{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39837980",
      "title": "Validating Input on Every Keystroke via State",
      "sourceHash": "439c2d2ece695d482ec38ae18f310a22d824f50396b6c1ac4d087c6ca54493ab",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.457,
          "end": 2.49,
          "en": "[Maximilian So now that we have a good idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.49,
          "end": 6.75,
          "en": "of how we can extract data when a form is submitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.75,
          "end": 11.75,
          "en": "let's explore form validation and input validation next.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "And when it comes to input validation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 18.69,
          "en": "as mentioned before in this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.69,
          "end": 21.48,
          "en": "you get a couple of different options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 21.48,
          "end": 25.17,
          "en": "For example, you can validate on every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.17,
          "end": 28.95,
          "en": "so whenever the user types into an input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 28.95,
          "end": 31.8,
          "en": "To show you how this could work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.8,
          "end": 35.94,
          "en": "I'll go back to the StateLogin form here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.94,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "So to the Login form that uses state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 42.78,
          "en": "because if we wanna react to every keystroke",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 42.78,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "and validate the value on every keystroke,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 48.66,
          "en": "we of course need to listen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.66,
          "end": 51.42,
          "en": "to all changes that are made to an input,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 51.42,
          "end": 54.72,
          "en": "and that is what we're doing here when using state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.72,
          "end": 57.633,
          "en": "and the handleInputChange function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.95,
          "end": 61.036,
          "en": "When using refs or when using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 61.036,
          "end": 66.036,
          "en": "the built-in FormData approach for extracting data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 66.24,
          "end": 68.31,
          "en": "we of course only have the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 68.31,
          "end": 73.11,
          "en": "once the form is submitted and not on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 73.11,
          "end": 76.08,
          "en": "So if you want to have keystroke validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.08,
          "end": 79.32300000000001,
          "en": "we need that stateful approach here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.64,
          "end": 84.21000000000001,
          "en": "Therefore, I'll go to App.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.21000000000001,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "and get rid of the Signup form import",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "and instead import the Login form again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 92.37,
          "en": "from the components folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 92.37,
          "end": 96.53999999999999,
          "en": "and there from the StateLogin.jsx file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 96.53999999999999,
          "end": 97.37299999999999,
          "en": "because I want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.37299999999999,
          "end": 100.74000000000001,
          "en": "that stateful version of that login form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 100.74000000000001,
          "end": 102.57,
          "en": "And then of course the login form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 102.57,
          "end": 105.513,
          "en": "should also be output here in the JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 107.52000000000001,
          "end": 111.03,
          "en": "Now, back in StateLogin.jsx,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 111.03,
          "end": 114.24000000000001,
          "en": "we can now validate the email input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 114.24000000000001,
          "end": 116.55,
          "en": "on every keystroke, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 119.763,
          "en": "by adding a computed value to this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 120.6,
          "end": 124.35,
          "en": "So that whenever the component function is executed again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 124.35,
          "end": 128.61,
          "en": "for example, because the email input changed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 128.61,
          "end": 131.64,
          "en": "we calculate a new value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 131.64,
          "end": 136.64,
          "en": "That value could be called emailIsInvalid, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138,
          "end": 141.48,
          "en": "and we might wanna store true or false in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.48,
          "end": 144.9,
          "en": "which we can then use down here in our form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.9,
          "end": 148.05,
          "en": "to update the look of this form",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.05,
          "end": 150.453,
          "en": "or to output an error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.53,
          "end": 155.7,
          "en": "And we can set this emailIsInvalid constant here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 155.7,
          "end": 159.213,
          "en": "based on this email state value which we're managing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 160.14,
          "end": 164.67000000000002,
          "en": "So here we could say that emailIsInvalid, should be true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 164.67000000000002,
          "end": 169.67000000000002,
          "en": "if the entered email does not include an at symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 170.55,
          "end": 172.95,
          "en": "For this we can use the includes method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 172.95,
          "end": 175.53,
          "en": "which is supported on every string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 175.53,
          "end": 178.74,
          "en": "and check if email does not include an at symbol",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 178.74,
          "end": 182.193,
          "en": "by adding an exclamation mark in front of this expression.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 183.39,
          "end": 186.21,
          "en": "So with that, we're checking if the entered email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 186.21,
          "end": 189.42,
          "en": "does not include the at symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 189.42,
          "end": 193.47,
          "en": "in that case, emailIsInvalid, would be true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 193.47,
          "end": 198.24,
          "en": "Now that we got this information, we can update the UI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 198.24,
          "end": 202.47,
          "en": "and therefore below the email input field",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 202.47,
          "end": 205.2,
          "en": "I'll add a new div, which I'll give a class name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 205.2,
          "end": 210.2,
          "en": "of control-error, which is a CSS class I prepared in advance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 211.59,
          "end": 213.48,
          "en": "in that index.css file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 213.48,
          "end": 216.303,
          "en": "which is already part of the starting project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 217.74,
          "end": 220.5,
          "en": "And here I wanna output an error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 220.5,
          "end": 223.653,
          "en": "if the email is invalid, so if this is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 225.09,
          "end": 229.05,
          "en": "Therefore down here we can output emailIsInvalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 231.99,
          "en": "and then output a paragraph if that is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 231.99,
          "end": 234.81,
          "en": "where I output some error message of my choice,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 234.81,
          "end": 236.43,
          "en": "like for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 236.43,
          "end": 241.43,
          "en": "Please enter a valid email address, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 243.84,
          "end": 246.15,
          "en": "If you now save that, you'll see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 246.15,
          "end": 250.51,
          "en": "that if you reload this page, we got this error message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 251.58,
          "end": 253.74,
          "en": "and this error message goes away",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 253.74,
          "end": 256.29,
          "en": "as soon as I add an at symbol,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 256.29,
          "end": 259.443,
          "en": "so as soon as I have a valid email address again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 260.34,
          "end": 262.77,
          "en": "But if I then invalidate this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 262.77,
          "end": 266.433,
          "en": "by removing the at symbol, the error message appears again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 267.81,
          "end": 271.053,
          "en": "So that's how we can validate on every keystroke.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 272.07,
          "end": 276.06,
          "en": "But of course this approach isn't perfect at the moment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 276.06,
          "end": 278.25,
          "en": "because this error message",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 278.25,
          "end": 281.55,
          "en": "is now showing up right from the start,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 281.55,
          "end": 285.183,
          "en": "and that might not be the behavior you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 290.67,
          "en": "Because you might want to at least give the user a chance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 290.67,
          "end": 292.86,
          "en": "of entering a correct value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 292.86,
          "end": 296.373,
          "en": "before you start showing error messages like this one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 298.71,
          "end": 300.81,
          "en": "Therefore, we might wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 300.81,
          "end": 305.81,
          "en": "that emailIsInvalid is only set to true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 306.21,
          "end": 309.423,
          "en": "if the user did start entering a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 310.65,
          "end": 312.78,
          "en": "And to make sure that this is the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 312.78,
          "end": 316.227,
          "en": "we could check if enteredValues.email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 318.99,
          "end": 322.68,
          "en": "is not equal to an empty string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 322.68,
          "end": 325.353,
          "en": "and it includes an at symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 326.4,
          "end": 331.4,
          "en": "So if it is equal to an empty string, this will be false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 331.95,
          "end": 334.44,
          "en": "It will not be marked as invalid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 334.44,
          "end": 338.40999999999997,
          "en": "because it's still that's starting value that we're seeing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 339.36,
          "end": 342.543,
          "en": "and therefore we don't wanna set this to true yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 343.53,
          "end": 346.74,
          "en": "Therefore, with this change made, if we reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 346.74,
          "end": 350.34000000000003,
          "en": "the error message is gone, but it appears as soon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 350.34000000000003,
          "end": 355.293,
          "en": "as I start typing until I do enter a valid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 357.06,
          "end": 360.3,
          "en": "But this solution also has two problems,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 360.3,
          "end": 364.29,
          "en": "for example, one problem is that if I did enter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 364.29,
          "end": 367.8,
          "en": "a valid email address, but I then erase it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 367.8,
          "end": 370.11,
          "en": "I'm not showing an error message here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 370.11,
          "end": 372.03,
          "en": "because we are checking",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 372.03,
          "end": 374.79,
          "en": "whether the email field is an empty string",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 374.79,
          "end": 378.663,
          "en": "in which case we will never set email is invalid to true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 379.68,
          "end": 382.38,
          "en": "Another problem which we'll face here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 382.38,
          "end": 384.51,
          "en": "is of course that yes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 384.51,
          "end": 387.42,
          "en": "we don't see an error message initially",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 387.42,
          "end": 392.25,
          "en": "but we do see one as soon as the user starts typing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 392.25,
          "end": 394.95,
          "en": "And of course, at this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 394.95,
          "end": 398.67,
          "en": "the user also didn't really have a chance",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 398.67,
          "end": 401.31,
          "en": "of entering a valid value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 401.31,
          "end": 403.71,
          "en": "So as mentioned before on the slide",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 403.71,
          "end": 407.17,
          "en": "we're showing the error message too early",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 408.03,
          "end": 413.03,
          "en": "and that's why we'll next explore validating on lost focus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 413.76,
          "end": 417.003,
          "en": "and how that could be a valid approach.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}